WEBVTT

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:32.160
Thank you.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:45.730
It says fiction.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.760
When we face reality,

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.210
We must be prepared to base our decisions on facts.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:10.840
In disaster situations, the need for accurate information is most immediate and crucial.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:15.710
Information comes from a variety of sources.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:20.880
It must be translated into facts that are meaningful to the user and his mission.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.470
This is not a complex process.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.500
It is part of everyday living.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.460
We use it when we cross the street.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:35.600
Check the weather.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.160
Determine the best way to fight a fight.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.270
Make an estimate of the situation.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:01:59.120
save a life.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.800
In each of these situations, a decision was made based on facts.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.330
And facts.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:11.930
Make.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:12.590
the difference.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:18.400
Without the facts, you may well find yourself in the position of a fire dispatcher.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.970
who received a frantic call.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:20.310
Help me!

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:26.450
Somebody, please. My house is in flames. My two children are trapped inside. Hurry, please, do something.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:31.450
Do something.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.550
That was the firefighter's job.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.260
They had the time, equipment, and personnel to save the children.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.000
But where would they go?

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.230
The woman failed to give her address to the dispatcher.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:43.170
A fact.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.100
She ignored.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.060
to understand the mechanics of getting the facts.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:48.770
Let us examine the steps.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:51.310
This includes collecting information.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:52.360
processing it.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.200
and disseminating the facts to those who need them.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:02:59.880
let's begin with the first step

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.590
collection of information.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:08.780
Any official of government has certain inherent responsibilities for the collection of information.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:12.790
To meet this responsibility,

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.920
A reporting system must be established within the framework of government.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.280
based on its existing resources.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.660
Information may be of a general and non-technical nature.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.240
which can be reported by anyone on a geographical basis.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.350
or technical information related to specialized function.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:40.200
which is reported by operating services such as police.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:49.300
public works.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:53.290
Agriculture.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:54.320
or

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.900
a shelter manager who may report information to the Emergency Operating Center.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:00.980
Thank you.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:06.720
Just as newspapers use reporters who are specialists in their fields,

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:07.830
like science

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:08.600
sports.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:09.290
politics.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:14.900
Government uses personnel assigned to each functional or technical area.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:16.310
to report the facts.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:25.160
get the information needed to make a decision on a specific problem.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:29.950
These people working together...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.540
gather information should be aggressive, accurate, reliable, and observant.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.200
They should know and understand people, facilities, areas, and communications.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:43.090
and they should cover both geographical and functional information.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.670
To be effective, people in this information system

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:58.350
should be organized, trained, equipped, and assigned well in advance of the emergency.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.830
They should be welded into a skillful team, for facts do make the difference.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:13.350
Everyone involved in emergency operations should be conscious of the need for accurate information.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:14.740
He should be alert.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:16.000
He should be aware.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:25.090
he should recognize that information flows to and from the various governmental departments already functioning.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:29.360
please.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:32.640
firemen.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.700
personnel of federal agencies.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:38.120
Industry.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.020
Public Utilities.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:43.620
public works.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.180
Community Shelters.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:54.160
Anyone or any situation can be a source of information.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:58.600
All persons involved must be trained to anticipate the need for...

00:05:58.820 --> 00:05:59.940
and recognize this

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.480
significance of information.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:11.360
Sometimes confusion arises in determining the difference between raw information and facts.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.100
This needn't be if raw information is questioned, investigated,

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:17.050
and validated.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:21.270
Raw information may not necessarily be factual.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.780
The difference is a matter of proof and verification.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:29.890
Information from a reliable

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.500
authoritative source can usually be trusted.

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:35.150
In this case, it is a matter of reliability.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:46.120
Trained people are needed not only to report occurrences, but to anticipate what might happen based on information they already have.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:51.250
example.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:58.000
An astute police officer observing a group of youths on the street late at night with nothing to do and no place to go.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:06:59.980
senses what might develop.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.140
to develop into a situation.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.690
He handles the situation in the right way.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.440
and at the opportune time.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.200
In doing so,

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:22.980
He uses his training and experience to anticipate and prevent possible trouble.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:27.700
This illustrates the value of recognizing the significance of a situation.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:38.720
In collecting information...

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:42.600
Everyone should understand and use the familiar five W's.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:44.660
essential in establishing facts.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:46.290
For example,

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:47.370
the people.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:50.910
have received a 10-Rentgen dose of radiation.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.950
by 7 p.m.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.690
in the Jefferson Park Shelter.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:04.300
because of fallout from an upwind nuclear explosion.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:12.800
The second step, processing, simply means transforming information into usable facts.

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:17.830
Incoming information is examined, sorted, and placed into the proper category.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:24.390
For example, data related to a particular area in a radiological situation is so labeled.

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:29.970
Every piece of information is examined to the-

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:39.560
its pertinence. For example, is it needed immediately? If so, by whom? Is it of future

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:54.020
value? If so, to whom? Is it a value to this government or to other governments? Processing

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:59.320
of information requires this examination to determine the reliability of its source. Is

00:08:59.320 --> 00:08:59.980
the source...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.080
is it completely reliable, fairly reliable, or unreliable, or cannot be judged?

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:13.810
Information must also be examined for its probability.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:20.070
Is it confirmed? Is it probably true? Is it improbable? Or can it be judged?

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:26.890
These and other questions must be answered.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.980
For example, if the information comes from a...

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:35.560
specialist in the field of law enforcement, medicine, fire, agriculture, is it likely there

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:41.720
is a basis of fact? Personal knowledge of the source of information helps determine its

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:50.780
reliability. Is what is vital to one department of government equally vital to another? Personal

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:54.400
knowledge of the significance of the information helps to determine its use.

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:05.610
Is the information reported realistic, feasible, and consistent with what is already known?

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:09.590
Personal knowledge of existing facts help determine its probability.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:13.680
Arriving at a decision is a deliberate and systematic process.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.480
Yet there's only one best way to function.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:17.640
Be thorough.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.580
Do the pieces of information fit together logically?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.940
so that the total picture comes into sharp focus.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.350
The gathering of all information

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:38.810
that is pertinent to a particular situation,

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.880
all the bits and pieces under one roof,

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.380
constitutes the basis for a factual estimate

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:46.200
of the situation.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.870
If some needed facts are missing, what then?

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:57.860
Questions relating to the evaluation of the situation

00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:59.900
are called essential elements.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:14.330
of information, or E-E-I. These questions must result in necessary answers. For example,

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:19.220
asking what are the limits of radiological contamination, though important, will not

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:24.310
provide the answers the leader needs to make a decision. It is not the essential element

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:29.970
of information. A better question would be where, how, and with what effect will radiological

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:41.520
contamination impede or deny operations. Another question, what roads are blocked

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:46.130
is of some value, but again does not give the answers required to make a

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:50.100
decision. The decision-maker is interested in those roads which are

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:56.710
important to his operation. A better question is where, how, and with what

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:59.970
effect will blocking of streets and highways impede operations?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:09.770
When the decision maker has the answers to the essential elements of information, he has a basis upon which to make judgment.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:18.900
When the information has been converted into facts, it must be made available to appropriate users.

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:20.480
Otherwise, it is useless.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:26.330
Provide these facts to those who need them.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:27.610
You need communications.

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:29.570
Messenger, telephone.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:51.670
For example, in addition to the warning given by sirens or other means,

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:56.120
information under emergency conditions can be communicated to the public

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:58.400
over the emergency broadcast system.

00:12:59.050 --> 00:12:59.970
People can be...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.700
warned of the potential radioactive fallout hazard and receive information about shelter

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:12.450
locations and the actions they should take to increase their chances for survival.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:29.930
Not only the public, but agencies.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.680
Emergency officials responsible for dealing with emergency conditions need factual information

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:39.180
both for field operations and headquarters decisions and direction.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:48.860
Thus, communications are vital to the dissemination of facts to those who need them and must use them.

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:57.110
The steps represented by this complete cycle provide the means to get the raw information,

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:59.970
establish the facts and get them to the point where they can...

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:06.290
can be used. The ability to develop useful facts from raw data is essential in this

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:15.040
process. The success of your decisions, survival actions taken by your community, will depend

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:21.730
on your knowledge, your alertness, your judgment. And successful decisions are based on facts.

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:29.810
Payoff is in terms of life. Your life.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:34.760
mind. Facts do make the difference.
